    "https://www.monash.edu/jobs/why-work-at-monash/benefits": {
      "title": "Benefits",
      "description": "Benefits - Jobs at Monash Home Courses Monash Online Library Donate Previous menu Toggle navigation Jobs at Monash Why work at Monash Why work at Monash Why work at Monash Benefits Benefits Healthy Workplace Healthy Workplace Campus life Campus life Job search at Monash Job search at Monash How to apply How to apply How to apply International applicants International applicants Career reflection Career reflection Searching for a job Searching for a job Applying for a job Applying for a job What to expect What to expect Preparing for an interview Preparing for an interview FAQs FAQs Trans and Gender Diverse Applicants Trans and Gender Diverse Applicants Inclusive workplace Inclusive workplace Policies & Procedures Policies & Procedures Contact Us Contact Us Skip to content Skip to navigation Home Home icon Monash Australia Monash Australia Monash India Monash Indonesia Monash Malaysia Monash Prato Monash Suzhou Monash Boston Hub Monash Australia Monash India Monash Indonesia Monash Malaysia Monash Prato Monash Suzhou Monash Boston Hub Courses Monash Online Library Donate Staff Staff Staff portal Intranet M-Space The Insider Staff Staff portal Intranet M-Space The Insider Students Students Student portal Student website Monash Connect Monash Online hub Students Student portal Student website Monash Connect Monash Online hub Alumni Alumni Alumni portal Alumni website Alumni Alumni portal Alumni website Search Menu Jobs at Monash Why work at Monash Benefits Healthy Workplace Campus life Job search at Monash How to apply International applicants Career reflection Searching for a job Applying for a job What to expect Preparing for an interview FAQs Trans and Gender Diverse Applicants Inclusive workplace Policies & Procedures Contact Us More Inclusive workplace Policies & Procedures Contact Us Toggle Search Close Close\n                        Search Search Why work at Monash Benefits Healthy Workplace Campus life You are here: Home | Why work at Monash | Benefits Benefits More than just work A range of on-site services are available at our campuses . Depending on your work location, this may include on-site gym, pool, bookshop, childcare, health service, food outlets, bank, post office, Oxfam etc. Staff can participate in cycling, yoga, pilates, aerobics and other classes before work, during lunchtime and after work at our Clayton, Caulfield and Peninsula campuses . Salaries We offer a range of competitive salaries, which we negotiate under the Enterprise Bargaining Agreement. Salaries are subject to annual incremental increases for most staff. Superannuation You'll typically receive the superannuation contributions, either the superannuation guarantee per cent (SG) or 17 per cent, depending on your tenure and fraction of appointment. Find out more about our policy. Salary Packaging A range of salary packaging options are available to you, including superannuation, laptops, gym membership and Monash University childcare centre fees. Staff Discounts You're eligible for various discounts on consumer products, included but not limited to travel and tourism, retail and banking, health insurance and Monash Sport memberships. Staff Development and Learning We have a strong commitment to staff development and learning. You can also apply for reimbursement of study fees and study leave, if you do an approved course that is relevant and beneficial to your role and career. See the Staff Professional Development Procedure. Supporting parents at work We are committed to supporting staff with caring responsibilities. We provide generous parental leave options and have a range of policies to promote workplace flexibility.\nWe have on campus childcare centres as well as parenting facilities.\nParents and carers can further benefit from attending workshops on managing transition to and from parental leave, including sessions for partners, irrespective of their gender. Supporting LGBTIQA+ Staff We recognise and celebrate the rich diversity of our community at Monash, including our lesbian, gay, bisexual, transgender and gender diverse, queer and questioning (LGBTIQA+) staff.\nTo cultivate an inclusive culture, Monash operates the Ally Network and have over 200 Allies among our staff, including HR staff. Resources surrounding LGBTIQA+ Staff Inclusion can be accessed via Staff Diversity and Inclusion unit.\nOur partner organisations understand the importance we place on inclusive practice -  their services and products are inclusive of LGBTIQ staff, their partners and families (e.g Bupa, Medibank Private, UniSuper). Car Leasing Novated car leasing is also available to eligible staff. Leave A wide range of leave options are available to you. A voluntary reduced working year scheme is also available if you wish to extend your leave options. Library Access As a staff member you have full access to extensive libraries and learning materials through the Monash University Library. Environmental Sustainability Monash University became a signatory to the UN Sustainable Development Goals (SDGs) in 2016 and committed to Net Zero Emissions by 2030. Our continuing commitment to the SDGs is demonstrated in our campus operations sustainability strategy. The Net Zero Initiative is an ambitious program of works aiming to transform the University’s campuses and operations to achieve net zero carbon emissions by 2030. Monash Club The Monash Club provides a vibrant, social, multi-purpose place to relax, meet, dine and/or work. Open weekdays from 8am for current and previous staff, Higher Degree Research (HDR) candidates, alumni and their guests. No membership fees apply. Parking and Transport Parking arrangements vary depending on where you work, but most locations have on-campus permit parking. You can also salary package your parking fees. Free shuttle buses run between campuses, and there are many public transport options to choose from. We also support staff cycling to work with bike parking facilities and a bike arrival station at Clayton campus. Recognition of Prior Service Your prior service at other Australian Universities or the public service, CSIRO and other institutions may be recognised for long service leave and other personal leave. Health, Wellbeing and Occupational Health and Safety We strive to provide a healthy and safe work environment for staff and we have a dedicated unit to promote a proactive safety culture within the University. We encourage our staff to pursue a healthy balance between work, family and other commitments. The Monash Wellbeing program promotes a healthy work-life balance that focuses on the following pillars of wellbeing: mind, body, work, culture, place and nutrition. Sport at Monash Monash Sport is your go-to facility on campus at Caulfield, Clayton and Peninsula for sporting facilities, services and programs. We provide a number of Free Play spaces, membership options - including a 3-Day free trial , staff discounts and free fitness and wellness event offerings throughout the year. TeamMONASH comprises students, staff, alumni, friends and family, who come together to represent us Monash. We acknowledge and pay respects to the Elders and Traditional Owners of the land on which our Australian campuses stand. Information for Indigenous Australians Community Faculties Locations Diversity and inclusion Safety and security Sustainability Resources Important dates How to apply A-Z index Policy Bank FAQs Contact Contact us Campus maps Jobs at Monash Recruit a student Pay online News Latest news Monash Lens Podcasts A Different Lens Monash Life On Our Site Who we are Find a course Find a researcher Partner with Monash Sitemap Community Faculties Locations Diversity and inclusion Safety and security Sustainability Resources Important dates How to apply A-Z index Policy Bank FAQs Contact Contact us Campus maps Jobs at Monash Recruit a student Pay online News Latest news Monash Lens Podcasts A Different Lens Monash Life On Our Site Who we are Find a course Find a researcher Partner with Monash Sitemap Registered Australian University ABN: 12 377 614 012 TEQSA Provider ID: PRV12140 CRICOS Provider Number Monash University: 00008C Monash College: 01857J Authorised by Executive Director, Marketing Website feedback Last updated: Nov 2023 Accessibility Disclaimer & copyright Terms & conditions Data privacy & cyber security Data Consent Settings Copyright © 2026 Monash University We use cookies to improve your experience, but you can choose which ones we use, and opt-out at any time. You can find more information in our Website Terms and Conditions Accept  all Cookie settings"
