    "https://www.monash.edu/jobs/how-to-apply/faqs": {
      "title": "FAQs",
      "description": "FAQs - Jobs at Monash Home Courses Monash Online Library Donate Previous menu Toggle navigation Jobs at Monash Why work at Monash Why work at Monash Why work at Monash Benefits Benefits Healthy Workplace Healthy Workplace Campus life Campus life Job search at Monash Job search at Monash How to apply How to apply How to apply International applicants International applicants Career reflection Career reflection Searching for a job Searching for a job Applying for a job Applying for a job What to expect What to expect Preparing for an interview Preparing for an interview FAQs FAQs Trans and Gender Diverse Applicants Trans and Gender Diverse Applicants Inclusive workplace Inclusive workplace Policies & Procedures Policies & Procedures Contact Us Contact Us Skip to content Skip to navigation Home Home icon Monash Australia Monash Australia Monash India Monash Indonesia Monash Malaysia Monash Prato Monash Suzhou Monash Boston Hub Monash Australia Monash India Monash Indonesia Monash Malaysia Monash Prato Monash Suzhou Monash Boston Hub Courses Monash Online Library Donate Staff Staff Staff portal Intranet M-Space The Insider Staff Staff portal Intranet M-Space The Insider Students Students Student portal Student website Monash Connect Monash Online hub Students Student portal Student website Monash Connect Monash Online hub Alumni Alumni Alumni portal Alumni website Alumni Alumni portal Alumni website Search Menu Jobs at Monash Why work at Monash Benefits Healthy Workplace Campus life Job search at Monash How to apply International applicants Career reflection Searching for a job Applying for a job What to expect Preparing for an interview FAQs Trans and Gender Diverse Applicants Inclusive workplace Policies & Procedures Contact Us More Inclusive workplace Policies & Procedures Contact Us Toggle Search Close Close\n                        Search Search How to apply International applicants Career reflection Searching for a job Applying for a job What to expect Preparing for an interview FAQs Trans and Gender Diverse Applicants You are here: Home | How to apply | FAQs FAQs Can I save my application and return later? Yes, you can save and exit your unfinished application and return later. Go to the Access your application page to continue your application. Please make sure your contact details are correct during the selection process. It’s important that we can contact you via email, telephone or post. Have you received my application? When you submit your application, you’ll receive an automatic acknowledgement email. If you don’t receive a response, please check the email address you provided is correct and check your Junk/Spam folder. The selection process can take some time. If you have a question about your application status, contact the person listed under 'enquiries' in the advertisement. Can I change or withdraw my application once I’ve submitted it? You can withdraw your application at any time via the Access your application page . You can change some fields on your application, but not all fields. For more information, contact the person listed under 'enquiries' in the advertisement. How can I get more information? Contact the person listed on the job advertisement under ‘enquiries’. Check the Monash University website for information about the Faculty or Portfolio and for a wide range of information about the University. What if I don’t have the right to work in Australia? We accept applications from overseas applicants. However, we must ensure applicants have the right to work in Australia by the time they start the job. This is to comply with the Department of Immigration and Border Control guidelines. Offers of employment to overseas applicants are subject to the Department of Immigration and Border Control granting approval for permanent residency or an appropriate temporary work visa to cover the period of employment. Applicants must notify the University of any Immigration Restriction that may preclude them from fulfilling the terms of any contract of employment offered by the University. More information is available from the Department of Immigration and Border Control . The contact person listed in the job advertisement can advise you about the possibility of an employer-sponsored visa. What if I'm currently living interstate or overseas? If you’re successful for an interview, we’ll discuss options for you to attend - either in person or remotely. We may provide travel and relocation assistance to new staff relocating from either interstate or overseas to work with us. The contact person listed in the job advertisement can advise whether assistance is available for the position. What are Monash salary rates? We offer a range of competitive salaries , which we negotiate under the Enterprise Bargaining Agreement. Salaries are subject to annual incremental increases for most staff. View salary rates: Academic staff salary rates Professional staff salary rates Trades and Services staff salary rates Teaching Associate Sessional and Casual Research Assistant rates Casual Professional Staff salary rates How is my personal information handled by Monash University? Monash values the privacy of every individual’s personal information and is committed to the protection of personal information. Your personal information is handled in accordance with the Privacy and Data Protection Act 2014 (Vic.) The Monash Recruitment Privacy Collection Statement sets out how the University handles your personal information for recruitment, engagement or other career related purposes. If your application is successful, Monash University will retain your information which will become part of your employment records. Please refer to the HR privacy collection statement for further details. If your application is unsuccessful, Monash University will retain your information on its database and may use this information to assess your suitability for other employment opportunities with the University. Should you wish to be removed from the database please email HR-Jobs@monash.edu with the words \"Remove from database\" in the subject line. How do I provide proof of work rights? When you accept an offer of employment at Monash, you may be asked to provide proof of work rights in Australia. You'll need to provide a certified copy of one of the documents listed below: Australian citizens A valid Australian passport An expired Australian passport and an Australian driver's licence An Australian citizenship certificate and an Australian driver's licence or photo ID An Australian birth certificate and an Australian driver's licence or photo ID A certificate of evidence of Australian citizenship and an Australian driver's licence or photo ID. Non-Australian citizens A valid passport What is a certified copy? A certified copy of a document is a photocopy of the original that has been declared true by an authorised person. Who can certify documents? For a list of people authorised to certify a document, please see this list . How to certify Take the original and a copy to an authorised person. The person will write on every page of the copy: “I have sighted the original document and certify this to be a true copy of the original.” The person will sign each statement and write their profession. For example, 'Pharmacist'. If you prefer, these documents can be sighted by a Monash University staff member in a fixed-term or continuing position. Why are we asking for this? Under Section 245 AB of the Migration Act 1958, Monash University has a legal obligation to ensure all employees have the right to work in Australia. We acknowledge and pay respects to the Elders and Traditional Owners of the land on which our Australian campuses stand. Information for Indigenous Australians Community Faculties Locations Diversity and inclusion Safety and security Sustainability Resources Important dates How to apply A-Z index Policy Bank FAQs Contact Contact us Campus maps Jobs at Monash Recruit a student Pay online News Latest news Monash Lens Podcasts A Different Lens Monash Life On Our Site Who we are Find a course Find a researcher Partner with Monash Sitemap Community Faculties Locations Diversity and inclusion Safety and security Sustainability Resources Important dates How to apply A-Z index Policy Bank FAQs Contact Contact us Campus maps Jobs at Monash Recruit a student Pay online News Latest news Monash Lens Podcasts A Different Lens Monash Life On Our Site Who we are Find a course Find a researcher Partner with Monash Sitemap Registered Australian University ABN: 12 377 614 012 TEQSA Provider ID: PRV12140 CRICOS Provider Number Monash University: 00008C Monash College: 01857J Authorised by Executive Director, Marketing Website feedback Last updated: Feb 2020 Accessibility Disclaimer & copyright Terms & conditions Data privacy & cyber security Data Consent Settings Copyright © 2026 Monash University We use cookies to improve your experience, but you can choose which ones we use, and opt-out at any time. You can find more information in our Website Terms and Conditions Accept  all Cookie settings"
