    "https://careers.pageuppeople.com/513/cw/en/job/697853/research-fellow-in-medicinal-chemistry": {
      "title": "Job Search",
      "description": "Job Search - Jobs at Monash Home Courses Monash Online Library Donate Previous menu Toggle navigation Jobs at Monash Why work at Monash Why work at Monash Why work at Monash Benefits Benefits Healthy Workplace Healthy Workplace Campus life Campus life Job search at Monash Job search at Monash How to apply How to apply How to apply International applicants International applicants Career reflection Career reflection Searching for a job Searching for a job Applying for a job Applying for a job What to expect What to expect Preparing for an interview Preparing for an interview FAQs FAQs Trans and Gender Diverse Applicants Trans and Gender Diverse Applicants Inclusive workplace Inclusive workplace Policies & Procedures Policies & Procedures Contact Us Contact Us Skip to content Skip to navigation Home Home icon Monash Australia Monash Australia Monash India Monash Indonesia Monash Malaysia Monash Prato Monash Suzhou Monash Boston Hub Monash Australia Monash India Monash Indonesia Monash Malaysia Monash Prato Monash Suzhou Monash Boston Hub Courses Monash Online Library Donate Staff Staff Staff portal Intranet M-Space The Insider Staff Staff portal Intranet M-Space The Insider Students Students Student portal Student website Monash Connect Monash Online hub Students Student portal Student website Monash Connect Monash Online hub Alumni Alumni Alumni portal Alumni website Alumni Alumni portal Alumni website Search Menu Jobs at Monash Why work at Monash Benefits Healthy Workplace Campus life Job search at Monash How to apply International applicants Career reflection Searching for a job Applying for a job What to expect Preparing for an interview FAQs Trans and Gender Diverse Applicants Inclusive workplace Policies & Procedures Contact Us More Inclusive workplace Policies & Procedures Contact Us Toggle Search Close Close\n                        Search Search You are here: Home | Job Search Job Search Applicant login Job alert Job Search e.g. Lecturer, Admin assistant Refine Search Categories Academic Academic - Research Only 1 Locations Campus Parkville campus 1 Work type Fixed-term (Full-time) 1 Faculty / Portfolio Faculty of Pharmacy and Pharmaceutical Sciences 1 Level / Salary Level A ($86,195 - $116,981) 1 New Search Research Fellow in Medicinal Chemistry Job No.: 697853 Location: Parkville campus Employment Type: Full-time Duration: 12 month fixed-term appointment Remuneration: $86,195 - $116,981 pa Level A (plus 17% employer superannuation) Amplify your impact at a world top tier Pharmacy and Pharmaceutical Sciences faculty Join our inclusive, collaborative community Be surrounded by extraordinary ideas - and the people who discover them The Opportunity An exciting opportunity has become available for a motivated and talented individual to join the Faculty of Pharmacy and Pharmaceutical Sciences as a Research Fellow in the Medicinal Chemistry Theme. The development of anti-malarial agents has been a significant research area within the Faculty. Reporting to Prof. Peter Scammells, the focus of the study will be the development of small molecule enzyme inhibitors which block the Malaria parasite’s ability to degrade haemoglobin and obtain amino acids needed for growth and survival. As a Research Fellow your main responsibility will be the synthesis, purification, characterisation and evaluation of novel PfM1 and M17 aminopeptidase inhibitors as well as other bioactive compounds acting at G protein-coupled receptors. This would include compound design, data management and analysis and sample preparation as well as a range of drug discovery-related activities. As the successful candidate you’ll have: A PhD in medicinal chemistry or organic chemistry Demonstrated experience in the design and synthesis of biologically active small molecules Proficiency in interpreting SAR data and applying it to compound optimisation Familiarity with ADMET principles and their influence on candidate progression A track record of peer-reviewed publication commensurate with your career stage Experience working within a team-based drug discovery or chemical biology environment, such as that found at MIPS An understanding of pharmacology and/or drug development will be highly regarded. This is an opportunity to contribute meaningfully to research that moves from molecule to medicine, working alongside a team with the infrastructure, industry partnerships, and scientific depth to make your progression real. Monash University seeks applicants for this opportunity who are able to demonstrate and present valid and current Australian work rights. About Monash University At Monash , work feels different. There’s a sense of belonging, from contributing to something ground breaking – a place where great things happen. We value difference and diversity , and welcome and celebrate everyone's contributions, lived experience and expertise. That’s why we champion an inclusive and respectful workplace culture where everyone is supported to succeed. Some 20,000 staff work for Monash around the world. We have 95,000 students, four Australian campuses, and campuses in Malaysia and Indonesia. We also have a major presence in India and China, and a significant centre and research foundation in Italy. In our short history, we have skyrocketed through global university rankings and established ourselves consistently among the world's best tertiary institutions. We rank in the world’s top-50 universities in rankings including the QS World University Rankings 2026. Together with our commitment to academic freedom , you will have access to quality research facilities, infrastructure, world-class teaching spaces, and international collaboration opportunities. Learn more about Monash . Today, we have the momentum to create the future we need for generations to come. Accelerate your change here. Monash supports flexible and hybrid working arrangements. We have a range of policies in place enabling staff to combine work and personal commitments. This includes supporting parents . To Apply Please submit a current copy of your resume along with a cover letter in which you address how you meet the key selection criteria in the position description. For further instructions on how to apply, please refer to ' How to apply for Monash Jobs '. Diversity is one of our greatest strengths at Monash. We encourage applications from Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander people, culturally and linguistically diverse people, people with disabilities, neurodivergent people, and people of all genders, sexualities, and age groups. We are committed to fostering an inclusive and accessible recruitment process at Monash. If you need any reasonable adjustments, please contact us at hr-recruitment@monash.edu in an email titled 'Reasonable Adjustments Request' for a confidential discussion. Your employment is contingent upon the satisfactory completion of all pre-employment and/or background checks required for the role, as determined by the University as well as you possessing current work rights for Australia . Enquiries: Prof. Peter Scammells, Professor of Medicinal Chemistry and Associate Dean Research, +61 (3) 9903 9542 Position Description: Research Fellow - MedChem Applications Close: Tuesday 22 September 2026, 11:55pm AEST Supporting a diverse workforce Back to search results Email Job Apply now Monash University recognises that its Australian campuses are located on the unceded lands of the people of the Kulin nations, and pays its respects to their elders, past and present. Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App Send me jobs like these We will email you new jobs that match this search. Great, we can send you jobs like this, if this is your first time signing up, please check your inbox to confirm your subscription. The email address was invalid, please check for errors. You must agree to the privacy statement Subscribe Recaptcha Privacy agreement Search results Position Location Level / Salary Closes Research Fellow in Medicinal Chemistry Parkville campus Level A ($86,195 - $116,981) 22 Sep 2026 Join the Faculty of Pharmacy and Pharmaceutical Sciences as a Research Fellow in the Medicinal Chemistry Theme working with the development of small molecule enzyme inhibitors. Current opportunities Position Location Level / Salary Closes Research Fellow in Medicinal Chemistry Parkville campus Level A ($86,195 - $116,981) 22 Sep 2026 Join the Faculty of Pharmacy and Pharmaceutical Sciences as a Research Fellow in the Medicinal Chemistry Theme working with the development of small molecule enzyme inhibitors. Powered by PageUp We acknowledge and pay respects to the Elders and Traditional Owners of the land on which our Australian campuses stand. Information for Indigenous Australians Community Faculties Locations Diversity and inclusion Safety and security Sustainability Resources Important dates How to apply A-Z index Policy Bank FAQs Contact Contact us Campus maps Jobs at Monash Recruit a student Pay online News Latest news Monash Lens Podcasts A Different Lens Monash Life On Our Site Who we are Find a course Find a researcher Partner with Monash Sitemap Community Faculties Locations Diversity and inclusion Safety and security Sustainability Resources Important dates How to apply A-Z index Policy Bank FAQs Contact Contact us Campus maps Jobs at Monash Recruit a student Pay online News Latest news Monash Lens Podcasts A Different Lens Monash Life On Our Site Who we are Find a course Find a researcher Partner with Monash Sitemap Registered Australian University ABN: 12 377 614 012 TEQSA Provider ID: PRV12140 CRICOS Provider Number Monash University: 00008C Monash College: 01857J Authorised by Executive Director, Marketing Website feedback Last updated: Nov 2022 Accessibility Disclaimer & copyright Terms & conditions Data privacy & cyber security Data Consent Settings Copyright © 2026 Monash University We use cookies to improve your experience, but you can choose which 