    "https://careers.pageuppeople.com/513/cw/en/job/698040/monashbayreuth-double-phd-degree-opportunity-accelerating-organic-semiconductor-discovery-with-generative-ai-molecular-dynamics-and-dft": {
      "title": "Job Search",
      "description": "Job Search - Jobs at Monash Home Courses Monash Online Library Donate Previous menu Toggle navigation Jobs at Monash Why work at Monash Why work at Monash Why work at Monash Benefits Benefits Healthy Workplace Healthy Workplace Campus life Campus life Job search at Monash Job search at Monash How to apply How to apply How to apply International applicants International applicants Career reflection Career reflection Searching for a job Searching for a job Applying for a job Applying for a job What to expect What to expect Preparing for an interview Preparing for an interview FAQs FAQs Trans and Gender Diverse Applicants Trans and Gender Diverse Applicants Inclusive workplace Inclusive workplace Policies & Procedures Policies & Procedures Contact Us Contact Us Skip to content Skip to navigation Home Home icon Monash Australia Monash Australia Monash India Monash Indonesia Monash Malaysia Monash Prato Monash Suzhou Monash Boston Hub Monash Australia Monash India Monash Indonesia Monash Malaysia Monash Prato Monash Suzhou Monash Boston Hub Courses Monash Online Library Donate Staff Staff Staff portal Intranet M-Space The Insider Staff Staff portal Intranet M-Space The Insider Students Students Student portal Student website Monash Connect Monash Online hub Students Student portal Student website Monash Connect Monash Online hub Alumni Alumni Alumni portal Alumni website Alumni Alumni portal Alumni website Search Menu Jobs at Monash Why work at Monash Benefits Healthy Workplace Campus life Job search at Monash How to apply International applicants Career reflection Searching for a job Applying for a job What to expect Preparing for an interview FAQs Trans and Gender Diverse Applicants Inclusive workplace Policies & Procedures Contact Us More Inclusive workplace Policies & Procedures Contact Us Toggle Search Close Close\n                        Search Search You are here: Home | Job Search Job Search Applicant login Job alert Job Search e.g. Lecturer, Admin assistant Refine Search Categories Academic Scholarship 1 Locations Campus Clayton campus 1 Work type Fixed-term (Full-time) 1 Faculty / Portfolio Faculty of Engineering 1 Level / Salary New Search Monash/Bayreuth Double PhD Degree Opportunity - Accelerating organic semiconductor discovery with generative AI, molecular dynamics and DFT Job No.: 698040 Location: Clayton (home) and Bayreuth (host) Study mode: Full-time Degrees: E8009.1 - Doctor of Philosophy (Monash - Bayreuth) Duration: 3.5-year fixed-term appointment Remuneration: AUD $37,145 per annum (tax-free stipend, 2026 full-time rate, pro-rata) About the Monash–Bayreuth Joint PhD Program The Doctor of Philosophy (Monash – Bayreuth) is an elite, international double-degree doctoral program delivered through a collaborative partnership between Monash University (Australia) and the University of Bayreuth (Germany). Designed to train the next generation of global research leaders, the program enables candidates to conduct cutting-edge research under joint supervision from both world-class institutions, culminating in a recognized double PhD degree. Monash University (Australia) Ranked 31st globally and a member of Australia’s prestigious Group of Eight, Monash is a powerhouse of research innovation. Its Department of Materials Science and Engineering ranks second nationally, driving breakthroughs in advanced materials, polymer chemistry, biomaterials, and metallurgy within state-of-the-art facilities. University of Bayreuth (Germany) A renowned center for interdisciplinary excellence, Bayreuth is globally recognized for its pioneering research in optical excitations, organic/inorganic semiconductors, macromolecular science, and advanced energy technologies. The International Joint Degree As part of this program (integrated within the DFG-funded IRTG 2818 / OPTEXC framework), candidates complete an extended research stay of 6 to 12 months at the partner institution. Doctoral researchers gain access to cross-continental industry links, specialized facilities, and dual academic networks, graduating with two doctoral degrees to maximize global career impact. The Research Opportunity This PhD project will explore how generative AI, molecular dynamics, and density functional theory (DFT) can be combined to accelerate the discovery and design of next-generation organic semiconductor materials with tailored optoelectronic properties. The project offers the opportunity to contribute to an emerging area of interdisciplinary research that brings together artificial intelligence and advanced materials modelling to address key challenges in semiconductor discovery. As part of the IRTG OPTEXC program, you will work at the intersection of generative AI, computational chemistry, molecular simulation and materials science, developing computational approaches to explore and predict new semiconductor materials and their properties. What makes this opportunity special? Earn a Doctor of Philosophy from Monash University and the University of Bayreuth (Germany). 12-month research stay in Germany - Undertake a fully funded 12-month research stay at the University of Bayreuth as part of the program. Who are we looking for? We are particularly interested in applicants with a background or experience in: • Computational chemistry • Materials simulation • Scientific machine learning / AI • Molecular dynamics or DFT • Materials science or a related discipline Successful applicants will also demonstrate: • Excellent academic and research capability • Strong written and verbal English communication skills • Strong problem-solving and communication skills • The ability to work independently and as part of a multidisciplinary research team. Qualifications • Applicants should hold, or be close to completing, a Bachelor Honours degree (H1 or equivalent) and/or Master's degree with an excellent academic record. • Candidates currently completing a 4-year Honours degree (or equivalent 3+1 year program) with a final-year research project, aiming for or achieving an H1 standard, will also be considered. • Applicants who already hold a PhD are not eligible. Degree Information • E8009.1 - Doctor of Philosophy (Monash - Bayreuth) Application Information Send a copy of your CV and cover letter detailing your suitability for this position to Dr Swarit Dwivedi swarit.dwivedi@monash.edu Applications Close: 30 November 2026, 11:55pm AEDT or earlier if the position is filled. Applications will be reviewed as they are received, and early applications are encouraged. Supporting a diverse workforce Back to search results Email Job Monash University recognises that its Australian campuses are located on the unceded lands of the people of the Kulin nations, and pays its respects to their elders, past and present. Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App Send me jobs like these We will email you new jobs that match this search. Great, we can send you jobs like this, if this is your first time signing up, please check your inbox to confirm your subscription. The email address was invalid, please check for errors. You must agree to the privacy statement Subscribe Recaptcha Privacy agreement Search results Position Location Level / Salary Closes Monash/Bayreuth Double PhD Degree Opportunity - Accelerating organic semiconductor discovery with generative AI, molecular dynamics and DFT Clayton campus 30 Nov 2026 As part of this program (integrated within the DFG-funded IRTG 2818 / OPTEXC framework), candidates complete an extended research stay of 6 to 12 months at the partner institution. Doctoral researchers gain access to cross-continental industry links, specialized facilities, and dual academic networks, graduating with two doctoral degrees to maximize global career impact. Current opportunities Position Location Level / Salary Closes Monash/Bayreuth Double PhD Degree Opportunity - Accelerating organic semiconductor discovery with generative AI, molecular dynamics and DFT Clayton campus 30 Nov 2026 As part of this program (integrated within the DFG-funded IRTG 2818 / OPTEXC framework), candidates complete an extended research stay of 6 to 12 months at the partner institution. Doctoral researchers gain access to cross-continental industry links, specialized facilities, and dual academic networks, graduating with two doctoral degrees to maximize global career impact. Powered by PageUp We acknowledge and pay respects to the Elders and Traditional Owners of the land on which our Australian campuses stand. Information for Indigenous Australians Community Faculties Locations Diversity and inclusion Safety and security Sustainability Resources Important dates How to apply A-Z index Policy Bank FAQs Contact Contact us Campus maps Jobs at Monash Recruit a student Pay online News Latest news Monash Lens Podcasts A Different Lens Monash Life On Our Site Who we are Find a course Find a researcher Partner with Monash Sitemap Community Faculties Locations Diversity and inclusion Safety and security Sustainability Resources Important dates How to apply A-Z index Policy Bank FAQs Contact Contact us Campus maps Jobs at Monash Recruit a student Pay online News Latest news Monash Lens Podcasts A Different Lens Monash Life On Our Site Who we are Find a course Find a researcher Partner with Monash Sitemap Registered Australian University ABN: 12 377 614 012 TEQSA Provider ID: PRV12140 CRICOS Provider Number Monash University: 00008C Monash College: 01857J Authorised by Executive Director, Marketing Website feedback Last updated: Nov 2022 Accessibility Disclaimer & copyright Terms & conditions Data privacy & cyber security Data Consent Settings Copyright © 2026 Monash University We use cookies to improve your experience, but you can choose which ones we use, and opt-out at any time. You can find more information in our Website Terms and Conditions Accept  all Cookie settings"
