    "https://careers.pageuppeople.com/513/cw/en/job/694500/associate-professor-regenerative-medicine": {
      "title": "Job Search",
      "description": "Job Search - Jobs at Monash Home Courses Monash Online Library Donate Previous menu Toggle navigation Jobs at Monash Why work at Monash Why work at Monash Why work at Monash Benefits Benefits Healthy Workplace Healthy Workplace Campus life Campus life Job search at Monash Job search at Monash How to apply How to apply How to apply International applicants International applicants Career reflection Career reflection Searching for a job Searching for a job Applying for a job Applying for a job What to expect What to expect Preparing for an interview Preparing for an interview FAQs FAQs Trans and Gender Diverse Applicants Trans and Gender Diverse Applicants Inclusive workplace Inclusive workplace Policies & Procedures Policies & Procedures Contact Us Contact Us Skip to content Skip to navigation Home Home icon Monash Australia Monash Australia Monash India Monash Indonesia Monash Malaysia Monash Prato Monash Suzhou Monash Boston Hub Monash Australia Monash India Monash Indonesia Monash Malaysia Monash Prato Monash Suzhou Monash Boston Hub Courses Monash Online Library Donate Staff Staff Staff portal Intranet M-Space The Insider Staff Staff portal Intranet M-Space The Insider Students Students Student portal Student website Monash Connect Monash Online hub Students Student portal Student website Monash Connect Monash Online hub Alumni Alumni Alumni portal Alumni website Alumni Alumni portal Alumni website Search Menu Jobs at Monash Why work at Monash Benefits Healthy Workplace Campus life Job search at Monash How to apply International applicants Career reflection Searching for a job Applying for a job What to expect Preparing for an interview FAQs Trans and Gender Diverse Applicants Inclusive workplace Policies & Procedures Contact Us More Inclusive workplace Policies & Procedures Contact Us Toggle Search Close Close\n                        Search Search You are here: Home | Job Search Job Search Applicant login Job alert Job Search e.g. Lecturer, Admin assistant Refine Search Categories Academic Academic - Teaching and Research 1 Locations Campus Clayton campus 1 Off-campus Other 1 Work type Continuing (Part-time) 1 Faculty / Portfolio Faculty of Medicine Nursing and Health Sciences 1 Level / Salary Level D ($181,629 - $200,092) 1 New Search Associate Professor - Regenerative Medicine Job No.: 694500 Location: Clayton Campus Employment Type: Part-time, fraction (0.8) Duration: Continuing appointment Remuneration: Pro-rata of $181,629 - $200,092 pa Level D (plus 17% employer superannuation) Amplify your impact at a world top 50 University Join our inclusive, collaborative community Be surrounded by extraordinary ideas - and the people who discover them The Opportunity As an Associate Professor in Regenerative Medicine, you will provide academic leadership across teaching, research and postgraduate education at ARMI. You will play a significant role within your discipline, contributing to its continued growth and reputation, while leading the Master of Biotechnology as Chief Examiner and Course Director and serving as Academic Head of the ARMI Student Program, encompassing HDR, Masters and Honours. This position focuses on the strategic development of the Student Program and is responsible for leading and delivering high-quality teaching across lectures, tutorials, practicals, workshops and other learning activities; developing innovative course materials and coordinating units, including supporting teaching staff and sessional academics. You will provide academic guidance and supervision to postgraduate, Honours and PhD students, oversee assessment and examinations, and contribute significantly to postgraduate training. You will also lead and undertake high-impact research, build collaborative research programs, publish in leading journals, attract competitive external and government funding, and contribute to research leadership. Through strong professional and disciplinary engagement, you will help advance the profile of regenerative medicine nationally and internationally, while actively supporting and aligning with the Institute’s culture, values and strategic priorities. To be successful in this role you will have a doctoral qualification and/or significant relevant experience, complemented by a distinguished record of scholarly and professional achievement. You will bring a strong publication record, success in securing external research funding, and demonstrated excellence in teaching, curriculum innovation and postgraduate supervision. You will be an accomplished mentor and academic leader, with strong interpersonal and collaborative skills and experience contributing to committees and academic administration. You will demonstrate the ability to build productive relationships, promote your discipline within the University and externally, and work collegially across multidisciplinary environments. About Monash University At Monash , work feels different. There’s a sense of belonging, from contributing to something groundbreaking – a place where great things happen. We value difference and diversity . That’s why we champion an inclusive and respectful workplace culture where everyone is supported to succeed. Some 20,000 staff work for Monash around the world. We have 95,000 students, four Australian campuses, and campuses in Malaysia and Indonesia. We also have a major presence in India and China, and a significant centre and research foundation in Italy. In our short history, we have skyrocketed through global university rankings and established ourselves consistently among the world's best tertiary institutions. We rank in the world’s top-50 universities in rankings including the QS World University Rankings 2026. Together with our commitment to academic freedom , you will have access to quality research facilities, infrastructure, world-class teaching spaces, and international collaboration opportunities. Learn more about Monash . Today, we have the momentum to create the future we need for generations to come. Accelerate your change here. Monash supports flexible and hybrid working arrangements. We have a range of policies in place enabling staff to combine work and personal commitments. This includes supporting parents . To Apply As part of your application, please submit the following documents: A Cover Letter outlining your motivation and aspiration for the role A CV (maximum 4 pages) with a full list of publications A Research Plan (maximum 5 pages) outlining your research direction and scientific plans for the initial 5 years in the role A statement on your philosophy of teaching (maximum 1 page) Diversity is one of our greatest strengths at Monash. We encourage applications from Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander people, culturally and linguistically diverse people, people with disabilities, neurodivergent people, and people of all genders, sexualities, and age groups. We are committed to fostering an inclusive and accessible recruitment process at Monash. If you need any reasonable adjustments, please contact us at hr-recruitment@monash.edu in an email titled 'Reasonable Adjustments Request' for a confidential discussion. Your employment is contingent upon the satisfactory completion of all pre-employment and background checks required for the role, as determined by the University. Enquiries: Professor Peter Currie, Director, Australian Regenerative Medicine Institute, Peter.Currie@monash.edu Position Description: Associate Professor Applications Close: Sunday 11 October 2026, 11:55pm AEDT Supporting a diverse workforce Back to search results Email Job Apply now Monash University recognises that its Australian campuses are located on the unceded lands of the people of the Kulin nations, and pays its respects to their elders, past and present. Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App Send me jobs like these We will email you new jobs that match this search. Great, we can send you jobs like this, if this is your first time signing up, please check your inbox to confirm your subscription. The email address was invalid, please check for errors. You must agree to the privacy statement Subscribe Recaptcha Privacy agreement Search results Position Location Level / Salary Closes Associate Professor - Regenerative Medicine Clayton campus, Other Level D ($181,629 - $200,092) 11 Oct 2026 As an Associate Professor in Regenerative Medicine, you will provide academic leadership across teaching, research and postgraduate education at ARMI. Current opportunities Position Location Level / Salary Closes Associate Professor - Regenerative Medicine Clayton campus, Other Level D ($181,629 - $200,092) 11 Oct 2026 As an Associate Professor in Regenerative Medicine, you will provide academic leadership across teaching, research and postgraduate education at ARMI. Powered by PageUp We acknowledge and pay respects to the Elders and Traditional Owners of the land on which our Australian campuses stand. Information for Indigenous Australians Community Faculties Locations Diversity and inclusion Safety and security Sustainability Resources Important dates How to apply A-Z index Policy Bank FAQs Contact Contact us Campus maps Jobs at Monash Recruit a student Pay online News Latest news Monash Lens Podcasts A Different Lens Monash Life On Our Site Who we are Find a course Find a researcher Partner with Monash Sitemap Community Faculties Locations Diversity and inclusion Safety and security Sustainability Resources Important dates How to apply A-Z index Policy Bank FAQs Contact Contact us Campus maps Jobs at Monash Recruit a student Pay online News Latest news Monash Lens Podcasts A Different Lens Monash Life On Our Site Who we are Find a course Find a researcher Partner with Monash Sitemap Registered Australian University ABN: 12 377 614 012 TEQSA Provider ID: PRV12140 CRICOS Provider Number Monash University: 00008C Monash College: 01857J Authorised by Executive Director, Marketing Website feedback Last updated: Nov 2022 Accessibility Disclaimer & copyright Terms & conditions Data privacy & cyber security Data Consent Settings Copyright © 2026 Monash University We use cookies to improve your experience, but you can choose which ones we use, and opt-out at any time. You can find more information in our Website Terms and Conditions Accept  all Cookie settings"
