    "https://careers.pageuppeople.com/513/cw/en/job/696407/research-assistant-in-rural-health": {
      "title": "Job Search",
      "description": "Job Search - Jobs at Monash Home Courses Monash Online Library Donate Previous menu Toggle navigation Jobs at Monash Why work at Monash Why work at Monash Why work at Monash Benefits Benefits Healthy Workplace Healthy Workplace Campus life Campus life Job search at Monash Job search at Monash How to apply How to apply How to apply International applicants International applicants Career reflection Career reflection Searching for a job Searching for a job Applying for a job Applying for a job What to expect What to expect Preparing for an interview Preparing for an interview FAQs FAQs Trans and Gender Diverse Applicants Trans and Gender Diverse Applicants Inclusive workplace Inclusive workplace Policies & Procedures Policies & Procedures Contact Us Contact Us Skip to content Skip to navigation Home Home icon Monash Australia Monash Australia Monash India Monash Indonesia Monash Malaysia Monash Prato Monash Suzhou Monash Boston Hub Monash Australia Monash India Monash Indonesia Monash Malaysia Monash Prato Monash Suzhou Monash Boston Hub Courses Monash Online Library Donate Staff Staff Staff portal Intranet M-Space The Insider Staff Staff portal Intranet M-Space The Insider Students Students Student portal Student website Monash Connect Monash Online hub Students Student portal Student website Monash Connect Monash Online hub Alumni Alumni Alumni portal Alumni website Alumni Alumni portal Alumni website Search Menu Jobs at Monash Why work at Monash Benefits Healthy Workplace Campus life Job search at Monash How to apply International applicants Career reflection Searching for a job Applying for a job What to expect Preparing for an interview FAQs Trans and Gender Diverse Applicants Inclusive workplace Policies & Procedures Contact Us More Inclusive workplace Policies & Procedures Contact Us Toggle Search Close Close\n                        Search Search You are here: Home | Job Search Job Search Applicant login Job alert Job Search e.g. Lecturer, Admin assistant Refine Search Categories Academic Academic - Research Only 1 Locations Monash Teaching Hospitals Monash Rural Health Bendigo 1 Work type Fixed-term (Part-time) 1 Faculty / Portfolio Faculty of Medicine Nursing and Health Sciences 1 Level / Salary Level A ($86,195 - $116,981) 1 New Search Research Assistant in Rural Health Job No.: 696407 Location: Any Rural Health Site: Bendigo, Gippsland, Mildura Employment Type: Part-time, fraction (0.6) - Full-time (0.9) - 0.9 FTE preferred, however fractions as low as 0.6 FTE will be considered based on the candidate’s experience and suitability Duration: 12-months fixed-term appointment Remuneration: Pro-rata of $86,195 - $116,981 pa Level A (plus 17% employer superannuation) Amplify your impact through research that advances rural health Join our inclusive, collaborative rural health research community Be surrounded by extraordinary ideas - and the people who discover them The Opportunity The School of Rural Health has an exciting opportunity for a Research Assistant to contribute to research across key rural health priorities, including workforce and training, service delivery, rural populations and First Nations health. The role will support defined research projects through literature and systems reviews, analysis of findings, and the preparation of reports, research materials and other documentation for the broader research team. Working within a collaborative research environment, the position will undertake research under limited supervision and contribute to research activities and administration. The role will participate in relevant meetings, provide advice to postgraduate students and support research that informs future approaches to rural health workforce, service delivery and population health. We are seeking someone with a doctoral qualification, or progress towards a doctorate, in a relevant discipline. Strong analytical, organisational and communication skills will support the preparation of research materials and reports, effective management of priorities and collaborative work. Computer literacy, attention to confidentiality and a willingness to learn new systems are also essential. Apply now to contribute to research with meaningful relevance to rural and regional communities. About Monash University At Monash , work feels different. There’s a sense of belonging, from contributing to something ground breaking – a place where great things happen. We value difference and diversity , and welcome and celebrate everyone's contributions, lived experience and expertise. That’s why we champion an inclusive and respectful workplace culture where everyone is supported to succeed. Some 20,000 staff work for Monash around the world. We have 95,000 students, four Australian campuses, and campuses in Malaysia and Indonesia. We also have a major presence in India and China, and a significant centre and research foundation in Italy. In our short history, we have skyrocketed through global university rankings and established ourselves consistently among the world's best tertiary institutions. We rank in the world’s top-50 universities in rankings including the QS World University Rankings 2026. Together with our commitment to academic freedom , you will have access to quality research facilities, infrastructure, world-class teaching spaces, and international collaboration opportunities. Learn more about Monash . Today, we have the momentum to create the future we need for generations to come. Accelerate your change here. Monash supports flexible and hybrid working arrangements. We have a range of policies in place enabling staff to combine work and personal commitments. This includes supporting parents . To Apply For instructions on how to apply, please refer to ' How to apply for Monash Jobs '. Your application must address the Key Selection Criteria. Diversity is one of our greatest strengths at Monash. We encourage applications from Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander people, culturally and linguistically diverse people, people with disabilities, neurodivergent people, and people of all genders, sexualities, and age groups. Your employment is contingent upon the satisfactory completion of all pre-employment and/or background checks required for the role, as determined by the University. Enquiries: Associate Professor Matthew Carroll, Matthew.Carroll@monash.edu Position Description: Research Assistant Applications Close: Thursday 10 September 2026, 11:55pm AEST Supporting a diverse workforce Back to search results Email Job Apply now Monash University recognises that its Australian campuses are located on the unceded lands of the people of the Kulin nations, and pays its respects to their elders, past and present. Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App Send me jobs like these We will email you new jobs that match this search. Great, we can send you jobs like this, if this is your first time signing up, please check your inbox to confirm your subscription. The email address was invalid, please check for errors. You must agree to the privacy statement Subscribe Recaptcha Privacy agreement Search results Position Location Level / Salary Closes Research Assistant in Rural Health Monash Rural Health Bendigo Level A ($86,195 - $116,981) 10 Sep 2026 Join as a Research Assistant in Rural Health and help improve health outcomes. Current opportunities Position Location Level / Salary Closes Research Assistant in Rural Health Monash Rural Health Bendigo Level A ($86,195 - $116,981) 10 Sep 2026 Join as a Research Assistant in Rural Health and help improve health outcomes. Powered by PageUp We acknowledge and pay respects to the Elders and Traditional Owners of the land on which our Australian campuses stand. Information for Indigenous Australians Community Faculties Locations Diversity and inclusion Safety and security Sustainability Resources Important dates How to apply A-Z index Policy Bank FAQs Contact Contact us Campus maps Jobs at 