    "https://careers.pageuppeople.com/513/cw/en/job/695634/senior-hr-business-partner": {
      "title": "Job Search",
      "description": "Job Search - Jobs at Monash Home Courses Monash Online Library Donate Previous menu Toggle navigation Jobs at Monash Why work at Monash Why work at Monash Why work at Monash Benefits Benefits Healthy Workplace Healthy Workplace Campus life Campus life Job search at Monash Job search at Monash How to apply How to apply How to apply International applicants International applicants Career reflection Career reflection Searching for a job Searching for a job Applying for a job Applying for a job What to expect What to expect Preparing for an interview Preparing for an interview FAQs FAQs Trans and Gender Diverse Applicants Trans and Gender Diverse Applicants Inclusive workplace Inclusive workplace Policies & Procedures Policies & Procedures Contact Us Contact Us Skip to content Skip to navigation Home Home icon Monash Australia Monash Australia Monash India Monash Indonesia Monash Malaysia Monash Prato Monash Suzhou Monash Boston Hub Monash Australia Monash India Monash Indonesia Monash Malaysia Monash Prato Monash Suzhou Monash Boston Hub Courses Monash Online Library Donate Staff Staff Staff portal Intranet M-Space The Insider Staff Staff portal Intranet M-Space The Insider Students Students Student portal Student website Monash Connect Monash Online hub Students Student portal Student website Monash Connect Monash Online hub Alumni Alumni Alumni portal Alumni website Alumni Alumni portal Alumni website Search Menu Jobs at Monash Why work at Monash Benefits Healthy Workplace Campus life Job search at Monash How to apply International applicants Career reflection Searching for a job Applying for a job What to expect Preparing for an interview FAQs Trans and Gender Diverse Applicants Inclusive workplace Policies & Procedures Contact Us More Inclusive workplace Policies & Procedures Contact Us Toggle Search Close Close\n                        Search Search You are here: Home | Job Search Job Search Applicant login Job alert Job Search e.g. Lecturer, Admin assistant Refine Search Categories Professional Human Resources 1 Locations Campus Clayton campus 1 Off-campus Mulgrave 1 Work type Continuing (Full-time) 1 Faculty / Portfolio Chief Operating Officer and Senior Vice-President 1 Level / Salary HEW 9 ($145,062 - $153,976) 1 New Search Senior HR Business Partner Job No: 695634 Location: 211 Wellington Road, Mulgrave and Clayton campus Employment Type: Full-time Duration: Continuing appointment Remuneration: $169,722 - $180,141 total remuneration package pa HEW Level 09 (inclusive of $145,062 - $153,967 base salary pa and 17% employer superannuation) Partner with extraordinary minds and leaders shaping tomorrow Key leadership role in a high-performing HR Business Partnering team Balance ambition and well-being through flexible, tailored working options. Monash University is a global leader ranked among the world's top universities. With annual revenue exceeding $3 billion and campuses across 5 countries, Monash combines the commercial scale, operational complexity, and rigor of a major global enterprise with a deeply values-driven mission. Learn more about Monash . The Opportunity We are seeking a Senior HR Business Partner to join our HR leadership ecosystem. Operating within a portfolio-based model supporting academic or professional divisions, this high-impact role requires strong coaching capability at senior/executive levels, alongside strategic advisory, organisational design, and industrial relations expertise to navigate complex environments while driving transformation. Key Responsibilities Executive Coaching & Advisory: Serve as a trusted advisor and senior coach to executive and senior leadership teams, guiding them through high-stakes decision-making, complex leadership dynamics, and the pursuit of strategic deliverables. Strategic Workforce Planning & Change: Lead organisational design, succession planning, and change across academic and/or professional portfolios. Translate business data into predictive workforce insights, forecasting talent needs, managing pipeline risks, and building an agile, future-ready workforce suited for growth, realignments, or shifting organisational realities. Complex Employee Relations & EA Navigation: Manage complex employee relations matters within an Enterprise Agreement (EA) environment. Partner with leaders and specialised ER teams to navigate industrial landscapes, mitigate risk, and champion constructive workplace relations. Enterprise HR Projects & Thought Leadership: play a key role on broader HR and university wide transformation projects. Bring fresh external insights, industry benchmarks, and progressive thought leadership to shape and deliver enterprise strategy. Innovation Champion: Role-model the adoption of AI tools and process optimisation. Challenge legacy thinking with \"outside-the-box\" solutions that elevate HR service delivery and operational effectiveness. Mentorship & Capability Building : Actively mentor and coach HR Business Partners and HR Advisors, elevating overall capability and fostering a culture of continuous learning across the HR function. About You We are looking for: Matrix Savvy & Systemic Thinker: Comfort and confidence navigating large-scale, complex matrix environments operating within an HR Shared Services and CoE model. Executive Presence & Coaching Mindset: High emotional intelligence, influence and interpersonal agility to build immediate trust, constructively challenge and coach senior leaders. Commercially Minded & Purpose-Led: Sharp business acumen balanced with an unwavering alignment to a values-driven, purpose-led culture. Digital Curiosity & Innovation: A forward-thinking, adaptable mindset with genuine enthusiasm for leveraging AI, tech optimisation, and creative problem-solving. Industrial & ER Expertise: Sound judgment and confidence navigating Enterprise Agreements, complex ER matters in unionised environments. Analytical & Evidence-Based: Strong data instincts with the natural ability to turn complex workforce metrics into clear, compelling strategic narratives. Collaborative leader: A genuine commitment to supporting and developing junior peers, sharing knowledge, and elevating overall team capability. About Monash University At Monash , work feels different. There’s a sense of belonging, from contributing to something groundbreaking – a place where great things happen. We value difference and diversity , and welcome and celebrate everyone's contributions, lived experience and expertise. That’s why we champion an inclusive and respectful workplace culture where everyone is supported to succeed Be part of our story. Work with us to #ChangeIt . Monash supports flexible and hybrid working arrangements. We have a range of policies in place enabling staff to combine work and personal commitments. This includes supporting parents . To Apply To apply, submit your CV along with a cover letter (maximum two pages) addressing your suitability to this position. Key Selection Criteria responses are not required. Please refer to ' How to apply for Monash Jobs' . Diversity is one of our greatest strengths at Monash. We encourage applications from Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander people, culturally and linguistically diverse people, people with disabilities, neurodiverse people, and people of all genders, sexualities, and age groups. We are committed to fostering an inclusive and accessible recruitment process at Monash. If you need any reasonable adjustments, please contact us at hr-recruitment@monash.edu in an email titled 'Reasonable Adjustments Request' for a confidential discussion. Your employment is contingent upon the satisfactory completion of all pre-employment and/or background checks required for the role, as determined by the University. Enquiries: Jo Dallas, Senior Manager Talent Acquisition, 9905 6121 Applications Close: Wednesday 9 September 2026 at 11:55PM AEDT Supporting a diverse workforce Back to search results Email Job Apply now Monash University recognises that its Australian campuses are located on the unceded lands of the people of the Kulin nations, and pays its respects to their elders, past and present. Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App Send me jobs like these We will email you new jobs that match this search. Great, we can send you jobs like this, if this is your first time signing up, please check your inbox to confirm your subscription. The email address was invalid, please check for errors. You must agree to the privacy statement Subscribe Recaptcha Privacy agreement Search results Position Location Level / Salary Closes Senior HR Business Partner Clayton campus, Mulgrave HEW 9 ($145,062 - $153,976) 9 Sep 2026 Join our dynamic Business Partnering team, where you will collaborate in a portfolio-based approach to deliver comprehensive HR services and advice, both operationally and strategically. Current opportunities Position Location Level / Salary Closes Senior HR Business Partner Clayton campus, Mulgrave HEW 9 ($145,062 - $153,976) 9 Sep 2026 Join our dynamic Business Partnering team, where you will collaborate in a portfolio-based approach to deliver comprehensive HR services and advice, both operationally and strategically. Powered by PageUp We acknowledge and pay respects to the Elders and Traditional Owners of the land on which our Australian campuses stand. Information for Indigenous Australians Community Faculties Locations Diversity and inclusion Safety and security Sustainability Resources Important dates How to apply A-Z index Policy Bank FAQs Contact Contact us Campus maps Jobs at Monash Recruit a student Pay online News Latest news Monash Lens Podcasts A Different Lens Monash Life On Our Site Who we are Find a course Find a researcher Partner with Monash Sitemap Community Faculties Locations Diversity and inclusion Safety and security Sustainability Resources Important dates How to apply A-Z index Policy Bank FAQs Contact Contact us Campus maps Jobs at Monas